From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: ahead read sync only around a cut through black (EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC_AUTO)

Our own work (read sync around cuts, 11 Nov; drafts-2026-11-11/ports-5/read-sync-around-cuts).
Patch 0583 in T131, after 0581 (lean SSBO) and 0582 (page range walk-ahead); no file in common with
either. The draft already carried 0583 (it had kept 0581/0582 for other drafts); the number stays.
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC_AUTO=<ms> (boot; 1 = 1500; 100-10000; off by default; needs
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD): with EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC off, 0567's read sync is armed from a black
frame until <ms> after the last black frame seen. EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC=1 still means always and
wins. Black test: a 64-point probe of the frame the renderer is about to show, copied with the
present's own commands and read at a later composite once the GPU is past it (never waits); black
= 56 of 64 points with every colour channel <= 16 of 255. New file
video_core/renderer_vulkan/present/black_probe.h; RendererVulkan gains a last member black_probe.
Off: one test of a boot value on the present thread and at each composite; OnCPURead's off path
keeps one load for Preflushable answers (the g_ahead load now comes first, the switch Peek after).
Ceiling: armed for more than 4 s with no lit (not black) probe read since arming (a long black or
dark stretch) disarms it, and it does not arm again until a lit probe is read. With the live
EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC on as well, the auto state is closed and reset at each present (one
"handed over" line if it was armed), so its lines never count the always-on time.
Lines: one per arm, disarm, cap and hand-over (at most 200 a run) and a 10 s
"EDEN_UP_AHEAD_READ_SYNC_AUTO 10 s" line (times armed and capped, presents armed, synced reads
while armed, longest armed stretch, probes). Probe cost while on: 64 one-pixel copies, two
barriers, a 256-byte read and, while a probe is pending, one GPU counter read per composite.
Without EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1 nothing is ever ahead, so the probe runs for nothing (small).
The port script's anchors in renderer_vulkan.cpp and renderer_vulkan.h still match once each.
Review fixes (review of the draft): (1) the probe refreshes the scheduler's known GPU tick
before its IsFree test, so a finished probe is read even when nothing else refreshed it (else all
four slots could stay pending and it would never arm); (2) the 4 s ceiling above, with a
"capped" line and a capped count in the 10 s line; (3) the third barrier (after the copy) is gone,
it guarded nothing; the comments say two barriers; (5) the live switch together with auto resets
the auto state; (6) the arm line's "black frame read M ms ago" is clamped at 0. Not taken: the
optional scheduler.WaitWorker() at shutdown (existing members have the same order).
